# What a real run reads to reach a real service instead of a fake. Copy this file to `.env.real`,
# which git ignores, and fill in only the services you want that run to meet.
#
#   bun run real:hetzner
#
# Nothing loads this file on its own, and that is the whole point of its name. Bun reads `.env` and
# `.env.test` into every `bun test`, so a token in either would make the plain command create real
# servers and spend money; `bun check` fails if either sets a variable this file names.
#
# See `docs/setups/hetzner-cloud.md`. A project that holds nothing else: the run makes its own
# firewall, labels everything it creates, removes all of it at the end, and removes what a killed
# run left behind, so anything still in that project afterwards is a leak.
HCLOUD_TOKEN=
